CloudBurrow patch 89 to github.com/goccy/googlesqlite v0.3.1
(cloudburrow/cloudburrow#1458). Applies after patch 0088; needs patches
0030, 0036 and 0065.

Patches 0030, 0056 and 0088 give a table made by tables.insert or a
CREATE TABLE statement the pseudo-column _PARTITION_STREAMED, the time
CloudBurrow's front streamed a row, which DML reads to refuse a row
streamed "within the last 30 minutes"
(https://cloud.google.com/bigquery/docs/data-manipulation-language). A
table made before those patches and kept in an instance's state had
none, so the front streamed to it without the time, and DML held its
streamed rows only while in the streaming buffer. The catalog's first
sync now gives every such table the column (SQLite ALTER TABLE ADD
COLUMN, and the catalog's spec, its updatedAt left as it is), NULL on the
rows it has, whose stream times were never recorded, so the rows streamed
to it from then on are held as BigQuery holds them. A temporary table, a
view, a change table and CloudBurrow's own tables get none, as before.
streamed_at_migrate_test.go fails without the patch and passes with it.

